[E0449] Error: `other` is lent for writing, and what it reaches is not kept
    ╭─[ err/426_keeps_refused/main.wip:11:39 ]
    │
 11 │     var fn take(other: &var Words) keeps other = {}
    │                                          ──┬──
    │                                            ╰──── a `&var` parameter
    │
    │ Note 1: what a `&var` argument reaches is lent for the call alone: its caller writes it again
    │
    │ Note 2: `keeps` names the parameters whose values a call may keep in its `&var` arguments, the receiver of a `var fn` among them
────╯
[E0449] Error: `text` is not a parameter of `add`
    ╭─[ err/426_keeps_refused/main.wip:13:30 ]
    │
 13 │     var fn add(word: str) keeps text = {}
    │                                 ──┬─
    │                                   ╰─── not a parameter
    │
    │ Note: `keeps` names the parameters whose values a call may keep in its `&var` arguments, the receiver of a `var fn` among them
────╯
[E0449] Error: `nowhere` has nothing to keep its arguments in
    ╭─[ err/426_keeps_refused/main.wip:16:44 ]
    │
 16 │ fn nowhere(text: str): str from text keeps text = text
    │                                            ──┬─
    │                                              ╰─── no `&var` parameter
    │
    │ Note: `keeps` names the parameters whose values a call may keep in its `&var` arguments, the receiver of a `var fn` among them
────╯
[E0449] Error: `collect` keeps `text`, and `Collect` does not say it may
    ╭─[ err/426_keeps_refused/main.wip:23:9 ]
    │
 19 │     var fn collect(text: str)
    │            ───┬───
    │               ╰───── declared here, keeping less
    │
 23 │     var fn collect(text: str) keeps text = self.words.push(text)
    │            ───┬───
    │               ╰───── keeps `text`
    │
    │ Note: a call through the interface keeps only what the interface's `keeps` names, so an implementation keeps no more
────╯
